> I wonder if there's a deeper synchronization issue in this. I. e. why was `tcp_resend_data()` called if there's no unacknowledged data?

To speed up the occurrence of this condition, I set ```tcp_rto = 50``` in tcp2.c.

To find out why tcp_resend_data() is called, I add debug message in the place where ```k_work_delayable_remaining_get(&conn->send_data_time)==0``` in tcp_in().
```
	if (!k_work_delayable_remaining_get(
		    &conn->send_data_timer)) {
		printk("%s: conn=%p send_data_total=%d unacked_len=%d send_timer.work.flags=0x%x(%s) uptime=%lld\n",
			__func__, conn, conn->send_data_total, conn->unacked_len, conn->send_data_timer.work.flags, 
			(conn->send_data_timer.work.flags & BIT(K_WORK_DELAYED_BIT)) ? "delayed" : 
			(conn->send_data_timer.work.flags & BIT(K_WORK_QUEUED_BIT)) ? "queued" : "", k_uptime_get());
		NET_DBG("conn: %p, Missing a subscription "
			"of the send_data queue timer", conn);
		break;
	}
```
Debug message when no data to send in tcp_send_data().
```
	len = MIN3(conn->send_data_total - conn->unacked_len,
		   conn->send_win - conn->unacked_len,
		   conn_mss(conn));
	if (len == 0) {
		printk("%s: conn=%p no data to send, thread='%s', uptime=%lld\n", __func__, conn, _current->name, k_uptime_get());
		ret = -ENODATA;
		goto out;
	}
```
The following is debug message printed in console. ```send_timer``` work has already been **_queued_** when ```k_work_delayable_remaining_get(&conn->send_data_time)==0```, and then the work is processed. The work is rescheduled again and again until the application calls zsock_send() to send new data and k_work_cancel_delayable() is called in tcp_in() when the ACK for the new data arrived.
```
tcp_in: conn=0x5689e9dc send_data_total=0 unacked_len=0 send_timer.work.flags=0x104(queued) uptime=4260
tcp_send_data: conn=0x5689e9dc no data to send, thread='tcp_work', uptime=4260
tcp_send_data: conn=0x5689e9dc no data to send, thread='tcp_work', uptime=4320
tcp_send_data: conn=0x5689e9dc no data to send, thread='tcp_work', uptime=4380
tcp_send_data: conn=0x5689e9dc no data to send, thread='tcp_work', uptime=4440
tcp_send_data: conn=0x5689e9dc no data to send, thread='tcp_work', uptime=4500
tcp_in: conn=0x5689e9dc send_data_total=0 unacked_len=0 send_timer.work.flags=0x104(queued) uptime=4980
tcp_send_data: conn=0x5689e9dc no data to send, thread='tcp_work', uptime=4980
tcp_send_data: conn=0x5689e9dc no data to send, thread='tcp_work', uptime=5040
tcp_send_data: conn=0x5689e9dc no data to send, thread='tcp_work', uptime=5100
tcp_send_data: conn=0x5689e9dc no data to send, thread='tcp_work', uptime=5160
tcp_send_data: conn=0x5689e9dc no data to send, thread='tcp_work', uptime=5220
```

Then I make k_work_cancel_delayable() be called when k_work_delayable_remaining_get()==0, tcp_send_data() will not be called and "no data to send" condition will not occur.
```
			if (!k_work_delayable_remaining_get(
				    &conn->send_data_timer)) {
				conn->send_data_retries = 0;
				k_work_cancel_delayable(&conn->send_data_timer);
				if (conn->data_mode == TCP_DATA_MODE_RESEND) {
					conn->unacked_len = 0;
				}
                		conn->data_mode = TCP_DATA_MODE_SEND;
				NET_DBG("conn: %p, Missing a subscription "
					"of the send_data queue timer", conn);
				break;
			}
```

Should we solve this synchronization issue and discard this pull request?

issue_context.body:
**Describe the bug**
When testing TCP stack, assertion fails as following:
```
ASSERTION FAIL [frag] @ /zephyr/zephyrmaster/zephyr/subsys/net/buf.c:640
@ /zephyr/zephyrmaster/zephyr/lib/os/assert.c:45
E: >>> ZEPHYR FATAL ERROR 4: Kernel panic on CPU 0
E: Current thread: 0x3d87e0 (tcp_work)
E: Halting system
```
The flow of this failure is:
```tcp_work thread``` -> tcp_resend_data() -> tcp_send_data()
```
{ 
        /* 1. send_data_totoal and unacked_len are all 0 in this case */
	len = 0 = MIN3(conn->send_data_total - conn->unacked_len,
		   conn->send_win - conn->unacked_len,
		   conn_mss(conn));

        /* 2. zero length packet (pkt->buffer=NULL) allocated */
	pkt = tcp_pkt_alloc(conn, len=0);
	ret = tcp_pkt_peek(pkt, conn->send_data, pos, len=0);

        /* 3. zero length packet passed to tcp_out_ext() */
	ret = tcp_out_ext(conn, PSH | ACK, pkt, conn->seq + conn->unacked_len);
}
```
-> tcp_out_ext() -> net_pkt_append_buffer(pkt, data->buffer=```NULL```) -> net_buf_frag_insert(..., buffer=```NULL```) -> _ASSERT_NO_MSG(frag) -> ```ASSERTION FAIL```

**To Solve**
Don't proceed if TCP resend length is zero.
```
	len = MIN3(conn->send_data_total - conn->unacked_len,
		   conn->send_win - conn->unacked_len,
		   conn_mss(conn));
	if (len == 0) {
		goto out;
	}
```

**Environment**
 - OS: Linux
 - Toolchain: Zephyr SDK
 - Commit 89212a7fbf5fcd8e4d661c016344ae4bf2d46f53

